the legendary creator of akira katsuhiro  otomo has created an animated  masterpiece three short stories woven  together as a sequence of memories today  we're going to talk about the second  part of the memories an episode called  stink bomb it's a satirical story about  a chemical researcher who is merely  seeking a solution to get rid of his  cold but why is everyone around him  dying let's dive into the film story to  find out what it's all about the film  begins with the picturesque views of  yamanashi and then the scenes  immediately shift to the waiting area of  a doctor's clinic swamped with patients  some of them are recurring patients it's  revealed that there's a flu outbreak in  the city the patient inside the doctor's  room is getting a flu shot by the nurse  the doctor recommends watching out for  his symptoms and that the shot would do  the trick he writes him a prescription  for the entire week the next patient who  walks inside has the flu too apparently  that year's flu breakout is bigger than  ever this man who just got his shot gets  dropped off at a lab he's nobuo a lab  technician battling the flu just like  any other person in the city nobody  decides to go back to the lab despite  the fever because he doesn't have  anything to do back at home and no one's  there to take care of him either nobuo's  colleague warns that he might set off  the biocon alarm if he sneezes too much  and suggests testing out the company's  over-the-counter cold medication maybe  take them all at once nobody has been  taking them but they're not helping  another colleague suggests he should try  the new medication the company is  working on since its samples are present  at the chief's desk two blue pills in  the red bottle should take care of the  flu  noble pays a visit to the chief's office  to show him some papers but he doesn't  find him there desperately trying to get  some relief he tries to find those pills  he reaches for the blue bottle since it  says samples and decides to take just  one of those red pills yeah you may have  taken the wrong ones two girls are  having a chat when they smell something  like perfume the chief comes out of his  office into the hall and starts yelling  he's found out that someone has stolen  the red pills the same colleague who  suggested nobody take the pills ended up  revealing that nobuo went inside the  office and took some of the samples upon  hearing this the chief gets even more  furious and asks where nobuo is they say  that he wasn't feeding well so he went  to the reception to take a nap the chief  reveals that it wasn't fever medication  and rushes to the reception to see how  nobuo is doing now others can smell  something unusual too nobuo wakes up  from a slumber feeling refreshed and  notices like it's morning and nobody  woke him up he steps into the hallway to  check and finds one of the girls  sleeping on a desk oh no it looks like  she's dead and it's not just her  everyone in the lab is dead even the  rats in the cages panicked by the site  he calls an ambulance he enters the  chief's room and finds out that he's  also dead it looks like the chief turned  off the biocon alarm but why would he do  that nobuo turns on the alarm and learns  that an incident has happened he's  connected to a video conference with  some folks who thought they related to  the chief and are surprised to see  someone else on the screen they're  asking for our maida the person in  charge the webcam rotates and the people  on the other end of the line are stunned  to find the boss on the floor nobuo  tells the man that everyone in the  facility has ended up like this and he's  not quite sure when all of this happened  and for how long nobody gets yelled up  for calling the police in the ambulance  none of them have shown up in this time  though he's asked to find a medication  and certain papers and bring them to the  tokyo headquarters the man behind the  screen is goichi ninasaki the head of a  new medicine development he's also  instructed not to give the medicine and  papers to anyone but him and tells him  to keep that accident discreet and to  not tell anyone that he works for the  company since all of this has something  to do with the pills the government  can't know anything about that mission  which is why he must find the papers and  medicine samples and get out of the lab  before the police find him the pills  happen to be part of a biological  weapons program being developed for the  government while people are dying  there's a strange view outside cherry  blossoms and sunflowers have bloomed at  the same time all plants in kofu city  are blooming the helicopter with a bunch  of reporters in the air is able to spot  a survivor it's none other than nobuo  swinging a flag to get their attention  as soon as they approach him the  repelling smell gets to them and they  fall down nobuo unaware of what's  happening uses the camera to call for  help garmada the president of nishibashi  pharmacy and the head of development  nirasaki explain everything to the  japanese military and that they're  trying to get data from chief omada's  computer to figure out how potent the  pill is the wind carrying the odor is  spreading the authorities think it's a  poisonous gas but they have yet to  determine what's causing it it takes a  while for kamata and nirasaki to figure  out that the only survivor nobuo is the  cause of the gas the men from the  military spot nobuo and try to approach  him to rescue him but they die from the  odor too it's clear to everyone that  nobuo is the stink bomb the officials  quickly withdraw from the scene no boy's  family sees him on tv asking for help  the head of the research company on the  other hand deduced that nobuo took the  pill and now he's a big threat to  everyone the sweat produced by his body  due to overwhelming emotions and body  movement is the reason why he stinks the  military wants him dead but others who  invested in the research want him alive  dozens of tanks helicopters and fighter  jets chase after nobuoa his grandmother  speaks on a loudspeaker from the  helicopter and tells him not to go to  tokyo then suddenly one of the soldiers  shoots at nobuo after trying to escape  he gets attacked by a huge number of  fighter jets tanks and even battleships  the missiles destroy roads bridges and  even houses he's on a scooter and oddly  enough he dodges all of the attacks  effortlessly it turns out that the  chemicals on nobuo's oda are causing  interference on the targeting systems  the rockets start going in the wrong  direction so the military's plan to kill  nobuo goes south  orders are given to evacuate tokyo at  this point there's chaos throughout the  city the traffic is jammed the airports  are crowded and the prime minister is  planning to release a statement asking  the un for help kamatar and nirasaki are  ordered to escape from the scene the u.s  military who've been watching the  situation up to this point takes over  the mission and sends in a nasa squad of  three soldiers in super powered space  suits to try to catch nobuo who they  wanna live  nasa's latest spacesuit is a prototype  which can repel electromagnetic  radiation and can help capture nobuo  alive nobuo scooter's given up and he  can't figure out why he's so hungry all  the time unaware of the mission the  japanese army destroys a section of the  bridge to prevent nobu from fleeing  locking him in a tunnel while using  liquid nitrogen wind repulsion devices  to try to freeze him meanwhile the nasa  squad wearing the prototype suits arrive  at the scene and try to approach the  stink bomb noble is frightened to see  these men but at this point he's got  nowhere to run  they managed to put him successfully  inside the isolation bag and drag him  back to the military headquarters in  tokyo one of the nasa soldiers brings  the suitcase full of documents and the  sample appeals to mr nirasaki after the  soldier presses the button on his suit  and one of the protective layers of his  helmet is removed they find out that the  person inside the suit is nobuo and he's  still completely unaware to the fact  that he's the cause of the biological  pollution he ejects himself out of the  exosuit killing everybody in the  facility  the end the film left us with so many  questions and we're sure you've got a  bunch of them yourself i mean how did  nobody make it all the way into the  command center without anybody noticing  him why didn't they make him take off  his costume before letting him in or at  the very least remove the tint why  hadn't it occurred to him that the odor  was actually coming from him all along  do you know the story for stingbomb is  based on an actual event it may be  referring to the gloria ramirez incident  causing toxic death tensai okamura  injects a much needed comedy into  memories lightening the tone and  throwing something completely unexpected  at the audience the dark humorous  moments paired against the all too real  sights of a viral outbreak add to the  overall feel of this one-of-a-kind  composition the main protagonist  fumbling antics as he thwarts the  government and army's advances never get  old and they always contribute to the  story's absurdity quotient stinkbomb is  a fantastic addition to this collection  of stories and one that you'll remember  for a long time if you enjoyed this  video be sure to check out the other two  stories part one and three of memories  for more videos like this follow our  channel and get updates about every new  video
 

